---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PolicyContact from "../../components/PolicyContact.astro";
import { brand } from "../../../brand.config";
import { resolveLocale, useTranslations } from "@/i18n/ui";

const t = useTranslations(resolveLocale(Astro.currentLocale));
---

<BaseLayout title={t("Policies.termsTitle")}>
  <div class="page-shell">
    <div class="page-shell__inner">
      <h1>{t("Policies.termsTitle")}</h1>
      <p><em>Last updated: September 2026</em></p>
      <p>
        This website is operated by {brand.name}. Throughout the site, the terms
        "we", "us" and "our" refer to {brand.name}. We offer this website,
        including all information, tools, and services available from {brand.siteUrl},
        to you, the user, conditioned upon your acceptance of all terms, conditions,
        policies, and notices stated here.
      </p>
      <p>
        By visiting our site and/or placing a wholesale inquiry or order with us, you
        engage in our "Service" and agree to be bound by these terms and conditions
        ("Terms of Service", "Terms"), including additional policies referenced
        herein or available by hyperlink. These Terms apply to all users of the site,
        including browsers, wholesale buyers, distributors, importers, and OEM/ODM
        project clients.
      </p>
      <p>
        Please read these Terms of Service carefully before accessing or using our
        website. By accessing or using any part of the site, you agree to be bound
        by these Terms. If you do not agree to all the terms and conditions of this
        agreement, you may not access the website or use any Services.
      </p>
      <p>
        Any new features or tools added to the site shall also be subject to these
        Terms. You can review the most current version at any time on this page. We
        reserve the right to update, change, or replace any part of these Terms by
        posting updates to our website. Your continued use of or access to the
        website following the posting of changes constitutes acceptance of those
        changes.
      </p>

      <hr />

      <h2>Section 1 – B2B service terms</h2>
      <p>
        By agreeing to these Terms, you represent that you are acting on behalf of a
        business (such as a retailer, distributor, or importer) and that you are at
        least the age of majority in your jurisdiction. Our Services are intended for
        B2B wholesale buyers — not for individual retail consumers unless explicitly
        agreed in writing. You may not use our products or Services for any illegal
        or unauthorized purpose, nor violate any laws in your jurisdiction (including
        copyright and trademark laws). You must not transmit malicious code or
        attempt to disrupt the Service. A breach of these Terms may result in
        termination of your access to our Services.
      </p>

      <h2>Section 2 – General conditions</h2>
      <p>
        We reserve the right to refuse Service to anyone for any reason at any time.
        You agree not to reproduce, duplicate, copy, sell, resell, or exploit any
        portion of the Service, product catalog, images, or website content without
        our express written permission. The headings in this agreement are for
        convenience only and do not limit these Terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Section 3 – Accuracy, completeness and timeliness of information</h2>
      <p>
        We are not responsible if information on this site is not accurate, complete,
        or current. Material on this site is provided for general information only
        and should not be relied upon as the sole basis for business decisions
        without confirming details with us directly. Catalog images, specifications,
        and availability may change. You agree that it is your responsibility to
        monitor changes to our site and to confirm order details before payment.
      </p>

      <h2>Section 4 – Modifications to the service and prices</h2>
      <p>
        Prices, MOQ, lead times, and product availability are subject to change
        without notice until confirmed in a written order or quote. We reserve the
        right to modify or discontinue the Service (or any part or content thereof)
        without notice. We shall not be liable to you or any third party for any
        modification, price change, suspension, or discontinuance of the Service.
      </p>

      <h2>Section 5 – Products and services</h2>
      <p>
        We supply ready-stock wholesale children's watches and custom OEM/ODM
        manufacturing services. Certain products may have limited quantities. Product
        colors and images are displayed as accurately as possible, but we cannot
        guarantee that your monitor or device will display colors exactly. We reserve
        the right to limit sales to any person, region, or jurisdiction and to limit
        order quantities. All product descriptions and pricing are subject to change
        without notice until your order is confirmed. Returns and refunds are
        governed by our <a href="/policies/refund-policy">Refund Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Section 6 – OEM/ODM custom orders</h2>
      <p>
        OEM/ODM orders are produced to your approved specifications, including
        branding, dial design, packaging, and other customization. You are
        responsible for confirming all specifications in writing before production
        begins and for ensuring that any logos, artwork, or brand assets you provide
        do not infringe third-party rights. Once production has started, the order
        cannot be cancelled and refunds are not available, even if goods have not yet
        shipped. Custom project terms, deposits, and lead times are confirmed before
        production.
      </p>

      <h2>Section 7 – Ready-stock wholesale orders</h2>
      <p>
        Ready-stock orders are fulfilled from existing inventory subject to
        availability at the time of confirmation. You are responsible for verifying
        model numbers, quantities, and shipping details before dispatch. Once goods
        have been shipped, returns and refunds are not available except as described
        in our <a href="/policies/refund-policy">Refund Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Section 8 – Orders, billing and account information</h2>
      <p>
        We reserve the right to refuse or cancel any order. We may limit quantities
        per buyer, company, or shipment address. Orders are confirmed after we verify
        stock or production capacity, pricing, shipping, and payment terms. You agree
        to provide current, complete, and accurate purchase, business, and shipping
        information, including import requirements for your destination country.
        Payment methods and schedules are agreed before production or dispatch. For
        more details, please review our{" "}
        <a href="/policies/refund-policy">Refund Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Section 9 – Third-party links and tools</h2>
      <p>
        Our Service may include links to third-party websites or tools (for example,
        payment processors, shipping carriers, or social media platforms) that we do
        not control. We are not responsible for examining or evaluating third-party
        content, and we do not warrant or assume liability for third-party materials,
        websites, or transactions. Your use of third-party services is at your own
        risk and subject to the third party's terms and policies.
      </p>

      <h2>Section 10 – Intellectual property and submissions</h2>
      <p>
        Our website content, product catalog, images, and trademarks remain our
        property or that of our licensors. If you send us feedback, ideas, or other
        submissions, you agree that we may use them without restriction or
        compensation, except where a separate written agreement applies. For OEM/ODM
        projects, you grant us the rights necessary to use your approved brand assets
        solely to fulfill your order. You are solely responsible for the accuracy and
        legality of materials you provide.
      </p>

      <h2>Section 11 – Personal information</h2>
      <p>
        Your submission of personal information through the site is governed by our{" "}
        <a href="/policies/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Section 12 – Errors, inaccuracies and omissions</h2>
      <p>
        Occasionally there may be information on our site or in the Service that
        contains typographical errors, inaccuracies, or omissions relating to product
        descriptions, pricing, MOQ, lead times, promotions, shipping charges, or
        availability. We reserve the right to correct any errors and to change or
        cancel orders if information is inaccurate at any time without prior notice
        (including after you have submitted an order). We undertake no obligation to
        update information except as required by law.
      </p>

      <h2>Section 13 – Prohibited uses</h2>
      <p>
        In addition to other prohibitions in these Terms, you are prohibited from
        using the site or its content:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>For any unlawful purpose or to solicit unlawful acts.</li>
        <li>To infringe our intellectual property rights or the rights of others.</li>
        <li>
          To submit false, misleading, or unauthorized brand assets for OEM/ODM
          production.
        </li>
        <li>To upload or transmit viruses or malicious code.</li>
        <li>
          To harass, abuse, spam, scrape, or collect personal information without
          consent.
        </li>
        <li>
          To interfere with or circumvent the security features of the Service.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We reserve the right to terminate your use of the Service for violating any
        prohibited uses.
      </p>

      <h2>Section 14 – Disclaimer of warranties; limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        We do not guarantee that your use of our Service will be uninterrupted,
        timely, secure, or error-free. The Service and all products delivered through
        the Service are provided "as is" and "as available" without warranties of any
        kind, either express or implied, except as expressly stated in your confirmed
        order. We are not liable for indirect, incidental, punitive, special, or
        consequential damages, including lost profits, resale market changes, or
        delays caused by customs, carriers, or events outside our reasonable control.
        In no case shall {brand.name}, our directors, officers, employees, affiliates,
        agents, contractors, suppliers, or service providers be liable beyond the
        maximum extent permitted by applicable law. Disputes should first be raised
        with us directly for resolution.
      </p>

      <h2>Section 15 – Indemnification</h2>
      <p>
        You agree to indemnify, defend, and hold harmless {brand.name} and our
        affiliates, partners, officers, directors, agents, contractors, suppliers,
        and employees from any claim or demand, including reasonable attorneys' fees,
        arising from your breach of these Terms, your violation of any law or
        third-party rights, or your use of the Service — including OEM/ODM brand
        assets or product specifications you provide.
      </p>

      <h2>Section 16 – Severability, termination and entire agreement</h2>
      <p>
        If any provision of these Terms is unlawful, void, or unenforceable, that
        provision shall be enforceable to the fullest extent permitted by law and the
        remainder shall remain in effect. These Terms are effective until terminated
        by you or us. We may terminate access if we believe you have failed to comply
        with these Terms. The failure of us to enforce any right or provision shall
        not constitute a waiver. These Terms, together with policies posted on this
        site, constitute the entire agreement between you and us regarding the
        Service.
      </p>

      <h2>Section 17 – Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms of Service and any separate agreements whereby we provide you
        Services shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of
        the People's Republic of China, without regard to conflict-of-law principles.
      </p>

      <h2>Section 18 – Changes to Terms of Service</h2>
      <p>
        You can review the most current version of the Terms of Service at any time
        on this page. We reserve the right, at our sole discretion, to update,
        change, or replace any part of these Terms by posting updates to our website.
        It is your responsibility to check our website periodically for changes. Your
        continued use of or access to the website or the Service following the
        posting of changes constitutes acceptance of those changes.
      </p>

      <PolicyContact />

      <p class="policy-related">
        Related:{" "}
        <a href="/policies/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a> ·{" "}
        <a href="/policies/refund-policy">Refund Policy</a> ·{" "}
        <a href="/policies/shipping-tax">Shipping &amp; tax</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
